  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Current version of Mulgara supported by Fedora 3.2.x is 2.1.1",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If using an external instance of Mulgara, there is a bug in the REST interface, XML entities in the result set are not correctly encoded as entities (eg \"&\" in a literal in a result appears as \"&\" not \"&amp;\") which results in mal-formed XML documents.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This is fixed in Mulgara 2.1.3  - ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://mulgara.org/release.html#v2.1.3"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://mulgara.org/release.html#v2.1.3",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This is not an issue that directly impacts Fedora (eg RISearch behaves correctly, SPARQL results format correctly includes the XML entity.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "However it does impact applications that want to directly query Mulgara using Mulgara's REST interface.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Presumably requires a Trippi upgrade as well.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
